     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. This order is double that maximum. It could cause serious toxicity, including lactic acidosis.\n\nThe order may have a typo. These are some possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day,** divided as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, at some other frequency.\n\nPlease tell me the dose you intended, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is truly what you want, tell me and give me a brief rationale for the order note. I'd still advise checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
